 'title' => 'What do you actually own when you own a share?',
 'excerpt' => 'A share makes you a part-owner of a company. Here is what that gives you, and what it does not.',
 'seo_description' => 'What owning a share really means: your rights as a shareholder, what you do and do not own, and where your shares are recorded in Nigeria.',
 'body' => '<p>When you buy a share, you buy a small slice of a company. That makes you a shareholder, which means you are one of the company\'s many part-owners.</p>
<h2>A slice of the company, not of its assets</h2>
<p>A company is a legal person in its own right. The factories, buildings, cash and equipment belong to the company, not to you personally. What you own is a share in the company itself. That share is a claim on its future profits, and a say in how it is run.</p>
<h2>What owning a share gives you</h2>
<ul><li><strong>A vote.</strong> Ordinary shareholders can vote on important matters at the company\'s Annual General Meeting (AGM), such as electing directors.</li><li><strong>A share of profits.</strong> If the company\'s directors declare a dividend, every share receives the same amount.</li><li><strong>A claim on what is left.</strong> If a company closes down, shareholders are paid only after the company\'s debts and other creditors have been settled.</li></ul>
<h2>What owning a share does not give you</h2>
<p>You cannot walk into the company\'s office and take a chair. You are not promised a dividend, because dividends depend on profit and on the directors\' decision. You are not promised a price either: the value of a share can go down as well as up.</p>
<h2>Where your ownership is recorded</h2>
<p>In Nigeria, listed shares are held electronically at the Central Securities Clearing System (CSCS) under your Clearing House Number (CHN). The company\'s registrar keeps the official list of shareholders. Your broker helps you buy and sell, but the shares are yours, not the broker\'s.</p>
<p>Understanding this one idea, that a share is ownership and not a loan or a savings product, makes every other part of investing easier to follow.</p>'
