<h2>Expectations matter more than news</h2>
<p>Investors buy and sell based on what they expect to happen. If they start to expect better profits, the price may rise before any results are published. If they start to worry, it may fall.</p>
<h2>The wider economy</h2>
<p>Changes in interest rates, inflation, the naira exchange rate, oil prices and government policy can affect many companies at once. A company can lose or gain value without doing anything differently.</p>
